  LanguageConfig_AbyssChallengeRuleDesc_CN = {
    Text = [[
<Title:"D-Effect Zone">
The D-Effect Zone is a high-difficulty gameplay system. Keepers need to flexibly assemble multiple challenge teams to acquire as much Training Points as possible for more rewards.

<Title:"Basic Rules of the Zone">
The D-Effect Zone is divided into 5 waves, each containing levels of varying difficulty.
Upon clearing a level, corresponding amounts of Training Points can be obtained, which can be viewed in the level detail interface.
When the Training Points reaches the specified requirement, in addition to receiving Silver and Black Offering, rare items "Gnosis Primer" and "Refined Gnosis Primer" can also be obtained! These are mysterious soul cores sourced from the depths of Mythag's Black Pool, which can help Awakeners increase their level cap, up to level 80!
The "D-Effect Zone" will periodically update the level content and rewards. After the current period ends, unclaimed rewards will no longer be obtainable, so Keepers should remember to complete and claim them on time~

<Title:"Special Rules of the Zone">
In the D-Effect Zone, there are unique restriction rules: the same Awakener and Posse, as well as the same Wheel of Destiny, cannot participate again. Keepers can flexibly choose their challenge team based on the initial Relic, monsters, and recommended levels.
Level II alarm levels will have their challenge team's combat abilities affected by the D-Tide, and specific effects can be viewed in the level detail interface.
After completing a challenge, if the Keeper finds a better team composition, they can use the "Reset" function to reset the challenge team for the corresponding level. Upon resetting, Awakeners, Posse, and Wheel of Destiny can re-enter, but the Training Points acquired from that level will be deducted (not affecting the reward status).
When Keepers repeatedly challenge the same wave's level, they must perform a reset first before proceeding with the challenge. This means that in each wave, a Keeper can obtain Training Points from only one level, and cannot collect it again.
In the "D-Effect Zone," one assistance can be used. The assistance Awakener and Wheel of Destiny will not be affected by the restriction rules; resetting a challenge team with assistance Awakener will also return one assistance chance.

<Title:"Leaderboard">
You can now check the current and previous Training Points leaderboards, as well as other Keepers' completion information in the D-Effect Zone, providing reference information for Keepers.
The leaderboard will display the highest Training Points and corresponding completion information for this period; resetting will not affect rankings, nor will it impact the display of completion team information.
]]
