  LanguageConfig_AbyssChallengeTipsV2_CN = {
    Text = "<Title:D-Effect Zone>\n\nThe D-Effect Zone is a high-difficulty gameplay system. Keepers need to flexibly assemble multiple challenge lineups to earn as many Training Points as possible and obtain more rewards.\n\n<Title:Basic Rules>\n\nThe D-Effect Zone is divided into 5 waves, each containing stages of varying difficulty levels.\nAfter clearing a stage, you can obtain the corresponding number of Training Points, which can be viewed in the stage details screen.\nOnce Training Points reach the specified requirements, in addition to claiming Silver Offering and Black Offering, you can also obtain the rare materials Gnosis Primer and Refined Gnosis Primer! These are mysterious Dream Cores produced from the Black Pool deep beneath Mythag, capable of raising an Awakener's level cap by up to level 90!\nThe D-Effect Zone periodically updates its stage content and rewards—generally once every 14 days. After the current period ends, any ongoing challenges from the previous period will immediately conclude, and unclaimed rewards will no longer be obtainable. Keepers, remember to complete and claim rewards in time~\n\n<Title:Special Rules>\n\nThe D-Effect Zone has its own unique restriction rules: the same Awakener and Posse, or Wheels of Destiny with the same name, cannot be fielded more than once. Keepers can flexibly choose their lineup for each challenge based on the starting Relics, enemies, and recommended level.\nAfter completing a challenge, if a Keeper finds a better combination, they can use the Reset function to reset the challenge lineup for the corresponding stage. After resetting, Awakeners, Posses, and Wheels of Destiny can be fielded again, but the Training Points earned from clearing that stage will also be deducted (this does not affect reward status).\nYou can use Support 1 time in the D-Effect Zone. The Support Awakener and Wheel of Destiny are not subject to the restriction rules. When resetting a challenge lineup that includes a Support Awakener, 1 use of Support will also be returned.\nDuring a challenge, you may use an Emergency Gnosis to assist with clearing. Each use consumes 3 Emergency Gnosis. Challenges completed after using one will be specially marked, and Training Point rewards can still be claimed normally, but they will not count toward the leaderboard.\n\n<Title:Extra Challenge>\n\nAfter clearing any stage, you can unlock that stage's Extra Challenge and face a higher-difficulty test.\nExtra Challenges require a separately assembled challenge lineup and are also subject to restriction rules: the same Awakener and Posse, or Wheels of Destiny with the same name, cannot be fielded more than once. Support uses are shared with normal challenges (1 use total across all modes).\nClearing an Extra Challenge grants 5 Training Points, which count toward the current period's total Training Points, helping you claim more rewards and improve your leaderboard ranking.\nYou can use the Reset function to separately reset the Extra Challenge lineup or the normal challenge lineup.\nIf you reset the normal challenge lineup after clearing the Extra Challenge, the Extra Challenge lineup will become the new normal challenge lineup, the Extra Challenge progress will be cleared, and the Extra Challenge Training Points will be deducted.\n\n<Title:Leaderboard>\n\nYou can now view the Training Points leaderboard for the current and previous periods, as well as other Keepers' clear information in the D-Effect Zone, providing reference intel for Keepers.\nThe leaderboard displays the Training Points and clear information at the time the highest Training Points for the current period were achieved. Resets will not affect rankings or the display of clear lineup information.\nPlease note that Training Points earned by clearing challenges using an Emergency Gnosis will be specially marked and will not count toward the leaderboard."
  },
