  LanguageConfig_LotteryRuleContent_CN = {
    Text = [[
1. "Colette's Flower House" has three gardens with the following opening times:
"Iris Garden": Opens on July 15 at 9:00 AM.
"Platycodon Flower Bed": Opens on July 17 at 9:00 AM.
"Rose Garden": Opens on July 19 at 9:00 AM.
2. Each exchange will consume 1,000 "Poems of Sorrow"/"Poems of Regret"/"Poems of Joy," randomly granting five item rewards from the garden.
3. The item rewards in each garden are divided into "Special Items" and "Common Items." When resetting, the remaining quantity of special items can be reset to the limit. The specific rules are as follows:
(1) For the first two resets: When there are no remaining "Special Items," the Keeper can choose to reset. After resetting, both the remaining quantities of "Special Items" and "Common Items" will be reset to the limit. Alternatively, they can continue exchanging. If there are no remaining "Common Items," a reset is required to continue exchanging.
(2) From the third reset onward: A reset can only be performed when there are no remaining "Common Items." This will reset the remaining quantity of "Common Items" to the limit, while "Special Items" will no longer reset.
4. After August 5 at 9:00 AM (GMT+8), any remaining "Poems" that have not been exchanged will be converted at a rate of 200 Poems for "Rose Scrip *5000." Keepers are advised to check their mails.]]
  },
