  LanguageConfig_PVPInstructions_CN = {
    Text = [[
<Title:[Traphase]>
 Traphase is a bonus game mode included with "Morimens". Each season, every card and the overall gameplay may undergo significant reworks and changes to create a more balanced and enjoyable game environment. Therefore, please be cautious about investing resources to unlock Traphase content.
<Title:[Matchmaking]>
 Traphase is a two-player competitive game that requires using the matchmaking feature to wait for a period of time to find a Rival. The matchmaking feature will prioritize finding a well-matched Rival to compete against you.
Simultaneous Matchmaking: Keepers can check both "All Pick" and "Draft Pick" to queue for multiple modes at the same time, which can effectively reduce the wait time to find a Rival.
Precision Matchmaking: Enabling this setting will search for a more evenly matched Rival, but it will increase the wait time to find a Rival. Disabling this setting will reduce the wait time to find a Rival, but the Rival may be relatively less evenly matched.
Simulated Rival: Enabling this setting will allow the system to assign a simulated Rival as needed during matchmaking, which reduces the wait time to find a Rival. Disabling this setting will only allow real players to be assigned as Rivals during matchmaking, which increases the wait time to find a Rival.
<Title:[Rankings]>
Score Rules: The starting score is 0. Keepers can earn points through ranked matches.
Score Changes: When both players have the same score, the winner will gain points equal to 5% of their total score, and the loser will lose the same amount.
Beginner Protection: When your score is below 1500, you will gain more points on a win and lose fewer points on a loss.
Strong Rival Challenge: Defeating a stronger Rival earns more points, while losing to a stronger Rival results in fewer points lost. Defeating a weaker Rival earns fewer points.
Independent Scores: "All Pick" and "Draft Pick" each have their own independent scores, but both follow the scoring rules described above.
<Title:[Season Updates]>
Season Reset: Under normal circumstances, the season resets every 28 days. After the reset, the portion of everyone's score exceeding 3000 will be halved.
Season Leaderboard: "All Pick" and "Draft Pick" each have their own independent seasons and season leaderboards. Season leaderboard rewards will be settled at the end of each season.
Leaderboard Eligibility: Participating in one match during the current season will place you on the season leaderboard for the corresponding mode, with your all-time high score during the season used as the ranking basis. Winning one match during the current season will qualify you to receive rewards based on your current season ranking at the end of the season.
Seasonal Mission: Both "All Pick" and "Draft Pick" have Seasonal Missions. Completing Seasonal Missions earns generous rewards. Seasonal Missions reset with each season update.
<Title:[All Pick]>
 "All Pick" is the foundational mode of Traphase. It uses a pre-prepared Lineup to compete against a Rival. Before matchmaking, you must select your Lineup to face a Rival with an Unknown Lineup.
<Title:[Draft Pick]>
"Draft Pick" is the advanced mode of Traphase. No pre-built team is required to queue. Before the battle begins, both players take turns selecting from a card pool containing Awakeners, Wheels of Destiny, and Posses to build their own Lineup for the subsequent match.
 In each match, the system will randomly select one Relic to take effect during the battle.]]
  },
