  LanguageConfig_RailWayResonanceRuleContent_CN = {
    Text = [[
1. There are richer Resonance enhancements in "Hectic Skybound Rail" to provide powerful assistance to Keepers during challenges.
2. Resonance Upgrade Materials can be obtained in "Wayfare Frames," and consuming these materials can activate Resonance effects.
3. Each phase will have Investigation Resonance events, and upon entering these events, you will gain powerful Resonance effects corresponding to that chapter, which will last until the end of the entire investigation.
4. The Resonance effect obtained in "Little N's Help" will last from the start of the investigation until its conclusion.]]
  },
  LanguageConfig_RailWayRulesContentV2_CN = {
    Text = "<Title:Overview>\n1. \"Hectic Skybound Rail\" is a continuous challenge mode using \"Astral Reign\" rules. Keepers will continuously challenge multiple final bosses from past Investigations across a variety of random encounters!\n2. The maximum Relic holding limit can be raised up to 36 in this mode.\n3. During the challenge, you can simultaneously possess and enhance 3 powerful \"Resonance\" effects from Investigations.\n4. Each Emergency Gnosis used reduces the VIP Points earned in this challenge by 20%.\n5. Exiting mid-challenge is supported with progress retained, but the lineup's State will not be updated to reflect external growth changes. Progress is retained for at most 7 days after the last challenge; if no challenge is continued during the retention period, the challenge is considered abandoned and progress will no longer be retained.\n\n<Title:Level Compensation>\nParticipating in \"Journey's Start\" grants level compensation. The specific rules are as follows:\n  ·Awakeners in the investigation lineup below level 60 will be compensated to level 60 for this challenge.\n  ·Awakeners in the investigation lineup with skill levels below level 5 will be compensated to level 5 for this challenge.\n  ·Awakeners in the investigation lineup with \"Madness Omen\" below level 6 will be compensated to level 6 for this challenge.\n  ·Awakeners in the investigation lineup with \"Soulforge Aptitude\" below level 5 will be compensated to level 5 for this challenge.\n  ·If the Keeper's level is below 60, it will be compensated to level 60 for this challenge.\n\n<Title:Stage Phases>\n1. A single challenge is divided into three phases in total. The theme enemies and Resonance effects for each phase are randomly generated within the corresponding range:\n  ·Phase 1: Corresponds to Chapters 1–4 of \"Faded Legacy\".\n  ·Phase 2: Corresponds to Chapters 5–8 of \"Faded Legacy\".\n  ·Phase 3: Corresponds to Chapters 1–4 of \"Astral Reign\".\n ·On Madness Difficulty, after completing the Phase 3 challenge, an additional Phase 4 final boss challenge against \"Tawil\" will begin.\n2. After defeating a phase boss, you can choose one from 3 random \"Chrono Pendulums\".\n\n<Title:Difficulty & Starting Relics>\nThis challenge features three difficulty levels. Each difficulty has different stage rewards and starting Relics. Keepers can review the detailed information before selecting a challenge difficulty.\n\n<Title:Stage Rewards>\n1. VIP Points can be earned by defeating Elites and Bosses across all difficulties. VIP Points are used to raise the \"Train Upgrades\" level to obtain rewards.\n  ·Phase 1: Defeat Elite/Boss to earn VIP Points ×25/75\n  ·Phase 2: Defeat Elite/Boss to earn VIP Points ×50/150\n  ·Phase 3: Defeat Elite/Boss to earn VIP Points ×75/225\n2. The higher the challenge difficulty, the more VIP Points you will earn.\n  ·[Hard Difficulty]: VIP Points earned from completing all three phases increased by 150%\n\n  ·[Madness Difficulty]: VIP Points earned from completing all three phases increased by 400%\n ·After defeating the final boss \"Tawil\", you can earn an additional 1500 VIP Points.\n\n<Title:Season Updates>\n1. The \"VIP List\" records Keepers who perform exceptionally in challenges. Keepers who challenge at least once per season and successfully earn VIP Points will be added to the \"VIP List\".\n2. The seasonal ranking of the \"VIP List\" is based on the most VIP Points earned in a single challenge and the fewest rounds used. Challenges can be repeated to improve rankings.\n3. After the season ends, the ranking rewards for the season's \"VIP List\" will be distributed via mail.\n4. Each season has Seasonal Missions. Completing Seasonal Missions grants abundant rewards. Seasonal Missions reset with each season update.\n5. During a season transition, stages still in progress can directly complete the latest Seasonal Missions upon finishing the challenge, but cannot enter the \"VIP List\"."
  },
  LanguageConfig_RailWayRulesContent_CN = {
    Text = "<Title:Gameplay Overview>\n1. \"Hectic Skybound Rail\" is a continuous challenge mode using \"Astral Reign\" rules. Keepers will face a series of final bosses from various investigation actions in unpredictable random encounters!\n2. The maximum Relic capacity can be increased up to 36.\n3. You can simultaneously possess and enhance powerful \"Resonance\" effects from 3 different investigation actions.\n4. Each use of Emergency Gnosis reduces the VIP Points obtained in this challenge by 20%.\n5. Mid-progress exit is supported and progress is retained, but the team status will not sync with external development. Progress is kept for up to 7 days after the last challenge; if not continued, progress will be forfeited.\n\n<Title:Level Compensation>\nParticipating in \"Train Departure\" provides level compensation as follows:\nIn the investigation team, Awakeners below Lv. 60 will be boosted to Lv. 60.\nIn the investigation team, Awakeners with Skill Levels below 5 will be boosted to Lv. 5.\nIn the investigation team, Awakeners with \"Frenzy Omen\" below Lv. 6 will be boosted to Lv. 6.\nIn the investigation team, Awakeners with \"Plasticity Adaptation\" below Lv. 5 will be boosted to Lv. 5.\nIf the Keeper's level is below 60, it will be boosted to 60 for this challenge.\n\n<Title:Phases>\n1. A single challenge is divided into three phases, with themed enemies and Resonance effects randomized within a specific range:\nPhase 1: Corresponds to Chapters 1–4 of \"Faded Legacy.\"\nPhase 2: Corresponds to Chapters 5–8 of \"Faded Legacy.\"\nPhase 3: Corresponds to Chapters 1–4 of \"Astral Reign.\"\n2. After defeating a Phase Boss, you can choose 1 of 3 random \"Chrono Pendulums.\"\n<Title:Difficulty and Initial Relics>\nThere are three difficulties, each with different stage rewards and initial Relics. Keepers can check details before selecting.\n\n<Title:Stage Rewards>\n1. Defeat Elites and Bosses to earn \"VIP Points,\" used to increase \"Lounge Specification\" levels for rewards.\nPhase 1: Elite/Boss victory grants 25/75 VIP Points.\nPhase 2: Elite/Boss victory grants 50/150 VIP Points.\nPhase 3: Elite/Boss victory grants 75/225 VIP Points.\n2. Higher difficulties provide more VIP Points.\n[Hard]: VIP Points earned +150% upon clearing all three phases.\n[Madness]: VIP Points earned +400% upon clearing all three phases.\n\n<Title:VIP Directory>\n1. The \"VIP List\" records Keepers with outstanding performance. Keepers who challenge once during the seacon and successfully earn VIP Points will enter the \"VIP List.\"\n2. Ranking is based on the highest VIP Points obtained in a single challenge and the lowest number of rounds used. You may challenge repeatedly to improve your rank.\n3. After the season ends, ranking rewards for this season's \"VIP List\" will be settled via mail.\n4. Each season features Season Missions that grant generous rewards upon completion. Season Missions reset with each season update.\n5. When seasons switch, stages still in combat can directly complete the latest Season Missions after the challenge ends, but cannot enter the latest \"VIP List.\""
  },
